From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:52:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] AP: lower unsolicited Link Measurement Report to debug

A client may send an RRM Link Measurement Report without the AP having an
outstanding request for it. hostapd logs that case at MSG_INFO, and with
logger_syslog_level=2 every such frame reaches syslog.

On the XR1710G (MT7996) one 5 GHz client sent them at roughly one per
second: all 980 hostapd lines in logread were this message, and the
128 KiB ring only held the first nine minutes after boot. The report is
not actionable - there is no request state to repair - so MSG_INFO is the
wrong level. Keep it visible only with -ddd as MSG_EXCESSIVE instead.

Logged in the r20 live review as N2 (syslog noise) / N9 (retention).

Local patch, not for upstream.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
--- a/src/ap/rrm.c
+++ b/src/ap/rrm.c
@@ -367,7 +367,7 @@ static void hostapd_handle_link_mesr_report(struct hostapd_data *hapd,
 
 	if (!hapd->link_mesr_req_active ||
 	    (hapd->link_measurement_req_token != report->dialog_token)) {
-		wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
+		wpa_printf(MSG_EXCESSIVE,
 			   "Unexpected Link measurement report, token %u",
 			   report->dialog_token);
 		return;
